 result←object ⍙Config arg;setting;value;from;to;dev
⍝ Read and/or write the DeltaWI configuration settings from a list of name-value pairs
⍝ Reading-only multiple names requires an extra level of nesting in order to make it look like shortened name-value pairs

 result←⍬ ⍝ Return the list of current or previous settings
 dev←1 ⍝? Override default developer setting while under construction
 :If 2=≢⍴arg ⋄ arg←↓arg ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ Allow a one- or two-column matrix instead of a vector of pairs
 :If 2≥|≡arg ⋄ arg←,⊂arg ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ Force it into a depth-3 vector of name-value pairs
 :For setting :In arg
     :If 1=≢setting←⊆setting ⍝ They're asking for the current value
         :Select ⎕C⊃setting
         :Case ⎕C'Debug' ⋄ result,←+/object ⎕VGET⊂'_Debug' 0
         :Case ⎕C'Developer' ⋄ result,←object ⎕VGET⊂'_Developer'dev
         :Case ⎕C'EWC' ⋄ result,←⊂object ⎕VGET⊂'_EWC' ''
         :Case ⎕C'EWCMode' ⋄ result,←⊂object ⎕VGET⊂'_EWCMode' 'Desktop'
         :Case ⎕C'Migration' ⋄ result,←⊂object ⎕VGET⊂'_Migration' ''
         :Case ⎕C'Pixels' ⋄ result,←⊂object ⎕VGET⊂'_Pixels' ''
         :Else ⋄ ##.##.Error'Domain Error'
         :EndSelect
     :Else ⍝ They're changing the current value (but return previous value)
         'Length Error'##.##.Error 2≠≢setting
         (setting value)←' '##.##.∆dlt¨setting
         :Select ⎕C setting
         :Case ⎕C'Debug' ⋄ result,←+/object ⎕VGET⊂'_Debug' 0
             :If 0=≢value←##.##.∆dtr value ⋄ value←0 ⋄ :EndIf
             :If ##.##.IsChar value ⋄ value←⌊⊃//⎕VFI value ⋄ :EndIf
             object._Debug←##.##.∆dim ##._supp.SetBitVals value ⍝ Debugging flags (integer vector of bit-values for convenient use with "∊")
         :Case ⎕C'Developer' ⋄ result,←object ⎕VGET⊂'_Developer'dev
             object._Developer←(1 0 '1' '0' 'T' 'F' 'Y' 'N' 2 '2'⍳⍥⎕C⊃value)⊃(8⍴1 0),2 2,dev ⍝ Developer (non-production) error-handling mode
             ⍝ Allow Developer=2 to mean that it also stops when ##.##.Error would produce a message
         :Case ⎕C'EWC' ⋄ result,←⊂object ⎕VGET⊂'_EWC' ''
             :If 0≠≢value ⋄ :AndIf '#.'≡2↑value ⋄ :AndIf 9=⎕NC value ⋄ :AndIf 3=(⎕VGET value).⎕NC'EWC' ⍝? Specify the EWC interface namespace to use
                 object._EWC_←⎕VGET object._EWC←value ⍝ Set up a link to the separate EWC support system
⍝? Also initialize the EWC system here, but we have to know what mode it will be in first
             :Else
                 object._EWC←'' ⋄ object._EWC_←⎕NULL
             :EndIf
         :Case ⎕C'EWCMode' ⋄ result,←⊂object ⎕VGET⊂'_EWCMode' 'Desktop'
             'EWCMode Domain Error'##.##.Error~(⊂value←1∘⎕C@(⍳×≢value)⎕C value)∊'' 'Desktop' 'Browser' 'Multi'
             object._EWCMode←value,(0=≢value)/'Desktop'
⍝? We need to re-initialize the EWC system with this new environment setting
         :Case ⎕C'Migration' ⋄ result,←⊂object ⎕VGET⊂'_Migration' ''
             ⍝ Does this look like a valid migration-support namespace?
             :If 0≠≢value←'.'##.##.∆dtr value ⋄ :AndIf '#.'≡2↑value ⋄ :AndIf 9=⎕NC value ⋄ :AndIf 4=(⎕VGET value).⎕NC'⍙_Each'
⍝? What happens if this namespace disappears during execution? Will translations just blow up, and is that OK?
                 object._Migration←value ⍝ Set up a pre-defined migration translation function connected to this namespace
                 (from to)←↓⍉↑'%'(≠⊆¨⊢)'#.'⎕R(value,'.')⍠'Regex' 0⊢_supp.apw_replacements
                 (from to)⊂⍛,⍨←'''[^'']*''|⍝.*' '&'
                 object._Translate←from ⎕R to ⍝ Predefine the translation function for use by ∇Requote
             :Else
                 object._Migration←''
                 object._Translate←⊢ ⍝ Otherwise assume there won't be any dynamic migration-translation
             :EndIf
         :Case ⎕C'Pixels' ⋄ result,←⊂object ⎕VGET⊂'_Pixels' 'Virtual'
             'Pixels Domain Error'##.##.Error~(⊂value←1∘⎕C@(⍳×≢value)⎕C value)∊'' 'Virtual' 'Real' 'Scaled' 'True'
             value←'Scaled' 'True'⎕R'Virtual' 'Real'⊢value ⍝ Allow undocumented synonyms
             object._Pixels←value←value,(0=≢value)/'Virtual'
             object._units[5;]←×⍣('V'≠⊃value)⊢object.DevCaps[4]÷100 ⍝ Adjust system 'units' to match
         :Else ⋄ ##.##.Error'Domain Error'
         :EndSelect
     :EndIf
 :EndFor
